            <physDesc xml:id="physDesc_b903f065">
               <titlePage label="" xml:id="titlePage_42e4a540">
                  <p xml:id="idm70">Johann Elias Schlegels | Werke, | Vierter Theil. | Herausgegeben | von | Johann Heinrich Schlegln, | Professor der Philosophie bey der Universität Kopenhagen, und | Secretär der königlich dänischen Kanzley. [emblem consisting of a lyre and a sceptre] | ___ | Kopenhagen und Leipzig, | In Verlage der Mummischen Buchhandlung. | 1766.</p>
               </titlePage>
               <titlePage label="Secondary title page (p. 220)" xml:id="titlePage_641208c3">
                  <p xml:id="idm72">Cantaten. | ___ | Der | Triumph der Ehre. Aus dem Metastasio. | ___ | </p>
               </titlePage>
               <extent xml:id="extent_1b9ac389">4 pages</extent>
               <watermark xml:id="watermark_262a810c">partly visible watermarks on the flyleaves hence indicating date of binding: 1) countermark or emblem 'J. Bassuet' with grapes above dating from the end of the eighteenth century or the beginning of the nineteenth century; 2) the second flyleaf has 'M DANG <rend xml:id="idm75" rend="sup">MOIS</rend>' (cf. Gravell:5722).</watermark>
               <physMedium xml:id="physMedium_d02daefd">In 8<rend xml:id="idm77" rend="sup">o</rend>; front endpaper, front flyleaf, title page (sig. [*1r]), blank page (sig. [*1v]), foreword (sigs. *2r–*3v), list of contents (sig. *4r–v), text (pp. 3–320), end flyleaf, end endpaper; in all 320 pages. The relevant pages concerning the present cantata are pp. 220–23 and a foreword pp. [205]–06.</physMedium>
